---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — bllog">
  <section class="shell page-intro narrow">
    <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
    <h1>A small place for clear thinking.</h1>
    <p>bllog is an intentionally simple editorial journal: strong typography, quiet surfaces, grayscale imagery and enough room around the content to let it breathe.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell about-grid">
    <div class="about-card">
      <h2>Editorial first</h2>
      <p>Posts live as Markdown and become static pages at build time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-card">
      <h2>Monochrome system</h2>
      <p>Black, white and neutral greys only. Glass is reserved for navigation and temporary controls.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-card">
      <h2>Small runtime</h2>
      <p>The site uses ordinary HTML for content and a tiny amount of JavaScript for theme switching and search.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-card">
      <h2>GitHub Pages ready</h2>
      <p>Every push to main validates, builds and deploys the static site automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
